

	Atari Lynx Steel Talons
	Control Summary
	Date:04/30/92

o Updates:

	o Player should not explode twice when continually getting shot.

	o Targetting system should now switch to lock on to closer target
	  if one enters into view.

	o Enemy Helicoptors (and jets) will now fly above all hills.

	o Enemy bullet firing should be more accurate (accuracy adjustment).

o Check out the final win sequence (when you survive all missions).

o Pass,Ace times per mission

	o Training     1:10   1:00
	o Mission 1    1:20   1:00
	o Mission 2    2:30   1:50
	o Mission 3    1:10   1:00
	o Mission 4    2:15   1:40
	o Mission 5    2:20   1:45
	o Mission 6    2:30   1:50
	o Mission 7    3:10   2:25
	o Mission 8    1:15   1:05
	o Mission 9    2:50   2:15
	o Mission 10   3:00   2:20
	o Mission 11   3:10   2:25
	o Mission 12   3:10   2:25

o Title Screen, Credits Screen, and High Score Screen (cycles every 5 seconds):

	o Pause: Pause game.

	o Pause+Option1: Restart game.

	o Pause+Option2: Flip.

	o A or B buttons: Go to Mission Select screens.


o Mission Select screens (timeout after 15 seconds--60 after 1st mission):

	o Pause: Pause game.

	o Pause+Option1: Restart game.

	o Pause+Option2: Flip.

	o A or B buttons: Start mission.

	o Up or Right on Joypad: Increase mission number.

	o Down or Left on Joypad: Decrease mission number.


o Game screen:
	
	o Pause: Pause game.

	o Pause+Option1: Restart game.

	o Pause+Option2: Flip.

	o A button:
		o Fire machine guns: Coin-op fire button 1.

	o B button pressed:

		o Option 1:
			o Zoom in and out: Coin-op zoom button.
		o Option 2:
			o Fire rockets: not on Coin-op.
		o Left on Joypad:
			o Turn facing to the left: Coin-op left foot pedal.
		o Right on Joypad:
			oTurn facing to the right: Coin-op right foot pedal.
		o Up on Joypad:
			o Increase altitude: Coin-op altitude lever up.
		o Down on Joypad:
			o Decrease altitude: Coin-op altitude lever down.

	o B button not pressed:

		o Option 1:
			o Bring up map screen.
		o Option 2:
			o Fire missiles: Coin-op fire button 2.
		o Left on Joypad:
			o Bank to the left: Coin-op joystick left.
		o Right on Joypad:
			o Bank to the right: Coin-op joystick right.
		o Up on Joypad:
			o Increase forward speed: Coin-op joystick forward.
		o Down on Joypad:
			o Decrease forward speed: Coin-op joystick back.

	o Note: Speed is auto centering to zero when going slow enough.


o Map screen (for as long as Option1 remains pressed):
	
	o Pause+Option1: Restart game.

	o A or B button (for as long as A or B button remain pressed):
		o Show locked target if any: Coin-op TV Close up.
